  Hans still trapped walking away dexhart  leaves a threatening voicemail for  dominic toretto as the car explodes  behind him with an impact that's still  being felt in the ninth film Hans death  both times is without a doubt the most  paused moment in the entire series it's  hard to remember a time when the fast  series wasn't the ridiculous basically  super heroic juggernaut it is today but  it's easy to figure out where the  turning point is Fast Five punched  audiences right in the face right from  its high-octane intro on a lonely desert  road the gang launches a daring assault  on a prison  the action slows to a dramatic crawl as  the bus flips over Brian's car and  careens along until we smash cut into  the title card this introduction is  simply brilliant Fast Five managed to  introduce its main players blast the  plot into overdrive and set the new  standard for its wild action all in  under 90 seconds if that wasn't enough  it also showed us that the past  franchise is apparently set in the same  universe as Parks and Recreation or at  least they cast the same actor who plays  perd hapley compared to the extremes the  franchise would go to later the bus  flipped pales in comparison but the raw  thrill of such a tightly paced opening  remains a highlight of the franchise  even when they're facing down seemingly  impossible odds that could lead to  certain doom Dom Toretto and his crew  very rarely show anything resembling  fear that is gotta go to work  in Furious 7 though there's one sequence  where they're definitely justified in  being a little worried we see them in a  dark space and then the floor opens up  to reveal they're in cars in the hold of  a cargo plane that does not seem to be  coming in for a landing any time soon  we've seen some insane stuff in the six  movies before this but would they really  go skydiving inside cars of course they  would  the vast franchise is full of ridiculous  stunts but nothing comes close to this  one why because 