 took the franchise in from there  like the tank catch Tom's big escape  plan from Furious 7 is a must pause  moment just not for the right reasons  after Tom rescues hacker Ramsey the bad  guy keeping her captive traps him  against the cliff with mercenaries on  one side and a sheer drop on the other  Tom smiles before launching into a  pretty sick burnout kicking up a cloud  of dirt that obscures everything a  reasonable person even in the fnf  universe might expect that Don would  escape in the confusion but that's not  nearly absurd enough for this movie he's  still there and all that dust was just  to spin his car around to face that clip  with that and with Ramsey making the  smart decision to put on a helmet Tom  floors it and goes over the cliff and  this time there's no parachute to slow  him down he seems to crash into every  rock along the way until finally the car  lands upside down and Tom emerges  brushing himself off and of course is  absolutely fine it's one way down a  moment you'll need to pause this moment  just to figure out what the hell  happened and how they're not dead that  must have been one heck of a good helmet  with all their talk about the importance  of family and the literal world saving  exploits of the later films it's easy to  forget that dominus crew or career  criminals the big heist at the end of  past five serves as a good reminder and  one of the  wildest sequences in the franchise Brian  and Dom have just ripped a 9,000 pound  steel vault onto the packed city streets  of Rio de Janeiro they've got it chained  to the respective car swinging it around  like a wrecking ball as they tear around  corners and smashing into the local cops  for collisions that are definitely not  going to leave a lot of survivors don't  worry though we're told that literally  every police officer in the city is  corrupt so that part's fine when they  take a sharp turn that sends the vault  careening into a crowded bank full of  terrified citizens how